KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ names a later non-throwing member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ names a later throwing member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Assertion 2 fails: W<int>::a() is taken as non-throwing.  The kept
noexcept-specifier is evaluated again when the class is complete
(implicit_exception_specifications), but for a class template
specialization without `this', so `b()' does not call W<int>::b.
Binding `this' there evaluated every member's specifier eagerly, which
instantiated unused templates (view_interface<take_view<int *>> for
`arr | views::take(3)') and broke cpp20_ranges_basic; [except.spec]/12
instantiates such a specifier only when it is needed.
